    description: "Pass 17 finding EEEEEE. analysis_runs[0..83].failed_files == [] for all 84 runs; analysis_runs[0..83].warnings == [] for all 84 runs. Known issues NOT reported: PPPPP (yaml analyzer processes 174 files producing 0 nodes from 173/174 — no warning); JJJJJ ('Not owner' Solidity require-msg propagating as language — no warning); the multiple linkers from MMMMMM (1+ seconds with zero productive output — no warning). Per-pass schema fields exist (failed_files: List[str], warnings: List[str]) but the channels are unused. Extends s14 YYYY (classification_failures=[] despite known mislabeling) and s14 RRRR (limits.skipped_passes 66 vs runs[].skipped_passes union 0)."  # cefc
    fields:  # cefc
      statement: "AnalysisRun.failed_files and AnalysisRun.warnings should report file-level errors and analyzer warnings encountered during a pass; universal emptiness across all 84 runs implies these fields are reserved-but-never-populated."  # cefc
      root_cause: "Each language analyzer reports its own failures/warnings through stdout/stderr or never reports them at all; the AnalysisRun structure exposes fields for these but no language analyzer populates them. The orchestrator never aggregates analyzer warnings into the structured record."  # cefc
